{
  "text": "I'll implement `svg.js` to the contract from the brief. First I'll read the brand spec, existing app files, and the knowledge-base dimension pages so the builders match tokens and real field numbers.Next I’ll pull the brand tokens, existing class names, and any remaining SVG spec so the library matches the app instead of inventing its own visual language.I have the tokens, class conventions, and real field distances. Next I’ll write `svg.js` as a single ES5 IIFE that implements the full `HRL_SVG` contract.I’ll scan `svg.js` for ES5 violations, block-level function declarations, and the other contract bugs I already spotted.Fixing strict-mode function declarations, the 11px font floor, radar draw order, strike-zone hotspots, and the grip inset.`svg.js` is in place as a single ES5 IIFE exposing `window.HRL_SVG` (and `module.exports` for Node). No shell was used; the reviewer should run `node --check svg.js` and the later test suite.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Names exported on `HRL_SVG`\n\n**Builders:** `field`, `strikeZone`, `basePaths`, `positionGrid`, `swingSequence`, `throwSequence`, `countMatrix`, `sprayChart`, `scaleGauge`, `radar`, `bar`, `timeline`\n\n**Vocabularies:** `POSITIONS`, `FIELD_PARTS`, `ZONE_CELLS`, `SWING_FRAMES`, `THROW_FRAMES`, `COUNT_CELLS`, `BUILDERS`\n\n**Helpers:** `hotspotLabel`, `positionName`, `positionNumber`\n\n---\n\n### 2. Builder options and default viewBoxes\n\nCommon to all: `title`, `desc`, `className`, `width` (viewBox width), `hotspots`. `opts` is optional; every builder returns a complete SVG with no arguments.\n\n| Builder | ViewBox | Options |\n|---|---|---|\n| `field` | 800×720 | `preset` `'t-ball'\\|'minor'\\|'major-ll'\\|'intermediate'\\|'junior'\\|'full'` (default `'major-ll'`); `showDimensions` bool; `labels` bool; `positions` bool; `positionStyle` `'number'\\|'abbr'\\|'both'` (default `'abbr'`); `alignment` `'standard'\\|'infield-in'\\|'dp-depth'\\|'bunt-defense'\\|'no-doubles'\\|'of-shallow'\\|'of-deep'\\|'corners-in'`; `unitColors` bool (default true when `positions`); `roles` `{p\\|c\\|1b\\|…: 'ball'\\|'base'\\|'backup'\\|null}`; `runners` `['first'\\|'second'\\|'third']`; `batter` `'R'\\|'L'\\|null`; `ball` `{x,y}` 0..1 or `'ss-hole'\\|'up-the-middle'\\|'right-center-gap'\\|'left-center-gap'\\|'down-the-line-left'\\|'down-the-line-right'\\|'shallow-center'\\|'deep-center'\\|'in-front-of-plate'`; `arrows` `[{from,to,style}]` with `style` `'throw'\\|'run'\\|'route'\\|'cut'`; `zones` bool; `covering` `{home\\|first\\|second\\|third: positionId}` |\n| `strikeZone` | 420×520 | `grid` `3\\|0` (default 3); `showBatter` `'R'\\|'L'\\|null`; `showZoneBox` bool (default true); `pitches` `[{x,y,call,n}]` with `call` `'ball'\\|'called-strike'\\|'swinging-strike'\\|'foul'\\|'in-play'`; `zoneRef` `'youth'\\|'adult'` |\n| `basePaths` | 600×560 | `runners` `[{from,to,style,label}]` with bases `'home'\\|'first'\\|'second'\\|'third'` and `style` `'force'\\|'tag'\\|'tag-up'\\|'steal'\\|'advance'`; `shade` `'force'\\|'tag'\\|null`; `leads` `[{base,type}]` with `type` `'primary'\\|'secondary'`; `labels` bool; `outs` 0–2 |\n| `positionGrid` | 720×260 | `highlight` position id |\n| `swingSequence` | 900×260 | `highlight` index or `'stance'\\|'load'\\|'stride'\\|'contact'\\|'finish'`; `order` array of those names; `showLabels` bool (default true); `hotspots` `frame-stance` … `frame-finish` |\n| `throwSequence` | 900×260 | same pattern for `'grip'\\|'separation'\\|'stride'\\|'release'\\|'follow-through'`; `showGrip` bool (four-seam inset); `hotspots` `frame-grip` … `frame-follow-through` |\n| `countMatrix` | 560×420 | `highlight` `'2-1'`-style; `shade` `'leverage'\\|null`; `hotspots` `count-0-0` … `count-3-2` |\n| `sprayChart` | 700×620 | `points` `[{x,y,type,outcome,label}]` with `type` `'ground'\\|'line'\\|'fly'\\|'pop'`, `outcome` `'hit'\\|'out'\\|'error'`; `showZones` bool (pull/centre/oppo) |\n| `scaleGauge` | 640×220 | `value` number (default 50); `compare` number; `label` string |\n| `radar` | 520×520 | `topics` `[{label,value}]` value 0..1; `rings` (default 4); `showValues` bool |\n| `bar` | 640×360 | `series` `[{label,value,color?,note?}]`; `max`; `unit`; `sort` bool |\n| `timeline` | 800×280 | `items` `[{label,sub,marker}]`; `highlight` index or label |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Vocabulary arrays (literal)\n\n```js\nFIELD_PARTS = [\n  'home', 'first', 'second', 'third', 'mound', 'plate', 'infield', 'outfield',\n  'foul-left', 'foul-right', 'fair-territory', 'warning-track', 'backstop',\n  'batter-box-left', 'batter-box-right', 'catcher-box', 'on-deck-left',\n  'on-deck-right', 'coach-box-first', 'coach-box-third', 'dugout-home',\n  'dugout-away', 'baseline-first', 'baseline-second', 'baseline-third',\n  'baseline-home', 'foul-pole-left', 'foul-pole-right', 'outfield-fence'\n]\n\nZONE_CELLS = [\n  'zone-1', 'zone-2', 'zone-3',\n  'zone-4', 'zone-5', 'zone-6',\n  'zone-7', 'zone-8', 'zone-9',\n  'zone-out-high', 'zone-out-low', 'zone-out-in', 'zone-out-away'\n]\n\nSWING_FRAMES = [\n  'frame-stance', 'frame-load', 'frame-stride', 'frame-contact', 'frame-finish'\n]\n\nTHROW_FRAMES = [\n  'frame-grip', 'frame-separation', 'frame-stride', 'frame-release', 'frame-follow-through'\n]\n\nCOUNT_CELLS = [\n  'count-0-0', 'count-1-0', 'count-2-0', 'count-3-0',\n  'count-0-1', 'count-1-1', 'count-2-1', 'count-3-1',\n  'count-0-2', 'count-1-2', 'count-2-2', 'count-3-2'\n]\n```\n\n`frame-stride` is in both swing and throw lists, as specified.\n\n---\n\n### 4. CSS classes emitted inside SVG markup\n\nRoot: `hrl-svg`, `hrl-svg-field`, `hrl-svg-strikeZone`, `hrl-svg-basePaths`, `hrl-svg-positionGrid`, `hrl-svg-swingSequence`, `hrl-svg-throwSequence`, `hrl-svg-countMatrix`, `hrl-svg-sprayChart`, `hrl-svg-scaleGauge`, `hrl-svg-radar`, `hrl-svg-bar`, `hrl-svg-timeline` (plus optional `opts.className`).\n\nHotspots: `hrl-hotspot`, `hrl-hotspot-hit`\n\nField: `hrl-field-park`, `hrl-field-fair`, `hrl-field-foul`, `hrl-field-warning`, `hrl-field-dirt`, `hrl-field-mound-dirt`, `hrl-field-infield-grass`, `hrl-field-mound`, `hrl-field-rubber`, `hrl-field-backstop`, `hrl-field-dugout`, `hrl-field-dugout-away`, `hrl-field-dugout-home`, `hrl-field-ondeck`, `hrl-field-box`, `hrl-field-coach-box`, `hrl-field-batter-box`, `hrl-field-catcher-box`, `hrl-field-line`, `hrl-field-fence`, `hrl-field-pole`, `hrl-field-base`, `hrl-field-plate`, `hrl-zone-foul`, `hrl-zone-of`, `hrl-zone-if`, `hrl-label-set`, `hrl-label`, `hrl-dim`, `hrl-dim-line`, `hrl-dim-label`, `hrl-runner`, `hrl-batter`, `hrl-ball`, `hrl-cover`, `hrl-cover-label`\n\nPositions: `hrl-pos`, `hrl-pos-{id}` (`hrl-pos-p` … `hrl-pos-rf`), `hrl-pos-token`, `hrl-pos-glyph`, `hrl-pos-label`\n\nRoles / arrows / legend: `hrl-legend`, `hrl-legend-roles`, `hrl-legend-item`, `hrl-arrow`, `hrl-arrow-throw`, `hrl-arrow-run`, `hrl-arrow-route`, `hrl-arrow-cut`, `hrl-arrow-force`, `hrl-arrow-tag`, `hrl-arrow-tag-up`, `hrl-arrow-steal`, `hrl-arrow-advance`, `hrl-arrow-head`, `hrl-arrow-tick`\n\nStrike zone: `hrl-sz-bg`, `hrl-sz-out`, `hrl-sz-box`, `hrl-sz-cell`, `hrl-sz-ref`, `hrl-sz-plate`, `hrl-sz-pitch`, `hrl-sz-batter`, `hrl-sz-legend`\n\nBase paths: `hrl-bp-bg`, `hrl-bp-diamond`, `hrl-bp-shade`, `hrl-bp-shade-force`, `hrl-bp-shade-tag`, `hrl-bp-shade-label`, `hrl-bp-runner`, `hrl-bp-runner-label`, `hrl-bp-lead`, `hrl-bp-lead-label`, `hrl-bp-outs`\n\nPosition grid: `hrl-pg-bg`, `hrl-pg-cell`, `hrl-pg-highlight`, `hrl-pg-num`, `hrl-pg-abbr`, `hrl-pg-name`, `hrl-pg-caption`\n\nSequences: `hrl-seq-bg`, `hrl-seq-frame`, `hrl-seq-highlight`, `hrl-seq-figure`, `hrl-seq-bat`, `hrl-seq-caption`, `hrl-seq-cue`, `hrl-grip-inset`\n\nCount: `hrl-count-bg`, `hrl-count-axis`, `hrl-count-cell`, `hrl-count-neutral`, `hrl-count-hitter`, `hrl-count-pitcher`, `hrl-count-highlight`, `hrl-count-walk`, `hrl-count-k`, `hrl-count-legend`\n\nSpray: `hrl-spray-wedge`, `hrl-spray-hit`, `hrl-spray-point`, `hrl-spray-legend`\n\nGauge: `hrl-gauge-label`, `hrl-gauge-track`, `hrl-gauge-tick`, `hrl-gauge-tick-label`, `hrl-gauge-band`, `hrl-gauge-marker`, `hrl-gauge-compare`\n\nRadar: `hrl-radar-ring`, `hrl-radar-axis`, `hrl-radar-poly`, `hrl-radar-dot`, `hrl-radar-label`, `hrl-radar-value`\n\nBar: `hrl-bar-row`, `hrl-bar-label`, `hrl-bar-track`, `hrl-bar-fill`, `hrl-bar-value`, `hrl-bar-note`\n\nTimeline: `hrl-tl-line`, `hrl-tl-item`, `hrl-tl-highlight`, `hrl-tl-marker`, `hrl-tl-label`, `hrl-tl-sub`\n\nTokens also set `data-role` / `data-teach` (`ball`, `base`, `backup`, `unit-if`, `unit-of`, `battery`) so the teaching-colour rules already in `styles.css` apply.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Field-dimension values (from the KB)\n\nSource: `youth-baseball-canada/wiki/concepts/field-dimensions-by-division.md`.\n\n| Preset key | Bases | Mound | Fence (min) | Maps to |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `t-ball` | 60 ft | **40 ft** | 200 ft | Rec T-ball bases (LL Tee Ball 60 ft). 40 ft pitching is Baseball Québec 11U Class B — the only 40-ft mound on that page. LL Tee Ball pitching is 46 ft. |\n| `minor` | 60 ft | 46 ft | 200 ft | Little League Minor (Rules 1.04–1.07: Tee Ball / Minor / Major and below) |\n| `major-ll` | 60 ft | **46 ft** | 200 ft | Little League Major (same 60/46 grid). Brief listed 50; the KB says 46. |\n| `intermediate` | 70 ft | 50 ft | 200 ft | Little League Intermediate (50-70) |\n| `junior` | 80 ft | 54 ft | 300 ft | Little League Junior **option** (default Junior is 90 / 60 ft 6 in) |\n| `full` | 90 ft | 60 ft 6 in | 300 ft | LL Junior/Senior default; BC 18U / 22U / Men’s |\n\nDefault preset is `major-ll`.\n\nStrike-zone copy follows the same KB: youth = LL armpits-to-top-of-knees; adult = OBR/BC letters (midpoint of shoulders and pants) to bottom of kneecap. Plate is labelled 17 in.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Deviations\n\n1. **`module.exports = root.HRL_SVG`**, not `window.HRL_SVG`. Required so `require()` works when `window` is undefined.\n2. **IIFE is invoked with `.call(...)`** so `this` is bound under `'use strict'` (bare invocation would make `this` undefined in Node).\n3. **`major-ll` mound is 46 ft**, not the brief’s parenthetical 50. 50 ft pitching is Intermediate (70 ft bases). Keys kept; numbers taken from the KB as instructed.\n4. **`t-ball` mound is 40 ft** as the brief’s API listed, mapped to the only 40-ft figure on the KB page (BQ 11U Class B). LL Tee Ball pitching is 46 ft.\n5. **`bar()` height grows above 360** when there are more than about six series so labels stay at ≥11px. A no-argument call is still 640×360.\n6. **Callers’ `opts` objects are shallow-copied** via local `extend()` so builders have no side effects.\n7. **Foul poles** use `var(--teach-ball, #dc2626)` (real foul-pole red/orange), not brand red, and only on the poles — turf/dirt/lines stay the specified neutrals.\n8. **No `node --check`** in this turn (shell was forbidden).",
